1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,110
Every team has had this moment: wait,

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:05,640
didn't we already decide not to do that?

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,870
Decisions live in meeting notes

4
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:09,120
and decision pages.

5
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,350
Months later, new work, or an AI

6
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:14,520
coding agent, quietly undoes them.

7
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,920
Precedent gives your team,

8
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,350
and your agents, a memory

9
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:20,072
of what has already been decided.

10
00:00:20,112 --> 00:00:21,872
There is no new process.

11
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:24,052
Teams keep typing /decision in their

12
00:00:24,092 --> 00:00:26,442
meeting notes and decision pages, or

13
00:00:26,482 --> 00:00:28,072
start a Jira comment with "Decision:".

14
00:00:28,112 --> 00:00:30,272
Precedent captures every decision,

15
00:00:30,312 --> 00:00:32,192
with its owner, date, rationale

16
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:34,872
and source, and shows right on the page

17
00:00:34,912 --> 00:00:36,702
which Jira work contradicts it.

18
00:00:37,723 --> 00:00:39,403
Here is a new work item:

19
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:42,363
move the payout ledger to MongoDB.

20
00:00:42,403 --> 00:00:43,393
Precedent checked it

21
00:00:43,433 --> 00:00:44,663
the moment it was written.

22
00:00:44,703 --> 00:00:46,963
It contradicts DEC-1:

23
00:00:47,003 --> 00:00:48,133
keep all transactional

24
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:50,123
payment data in PostgreSQL.

25
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:52,003
It shows the exact sentence

26
00:00:52,043 --> 00:00:53,243
that tripped the guardrail,

27
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:55,993
who decided, when, and where.

28
00:00:56,033 --> 00:00:57,713
It works live.

29
00:00:57,753 --> 00:00:59,553
Here is a brand-new work item:

30
00:00:59,593 --> 00:01:02,113
integrate Adyen for EU card payments.

31
00:01:02,153 --> 00:01:03,813
The moment it is created,

32
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:04,993
Precedent flags it against

33
00:01:05,033 --> 00:01:07,173
the decision to standardize on Stripe,

34
00:01:07,213 --> 00:01:08,433
owned by Dana Kim.

35
00:01:08,473 --> 00:01:10,533
And it understands direction:

36
00:01:10,573 --> 00:01:12,403
removing MongoDB from the refunds

37
00:01:12,443 --> 00:01:13,543
service is aligned

38
00:01:13,583 --> 00:01:15,943
with the decision, not a conflict.

39
00:01:16,542 --> 00:01:17,762
Ask Precedent hands

40
00:01:17,802 --> 00:01:20,062
the context to the Rovo agent.

41
00:01:20,102 --> 00:01:22,282
It explains why the decision was made,

42
00:01:22,322 --> 00:01:24,242
who to talk to, and the options:

43
00:01:24,282 --> 00:01:26,942
comply, log an exception with a reason,

44
00:01:26,982 --> 00:01:28,902
or supersede the decision.

45
00:01:28,942 --> 00:01:30,952
Every answer cites the decision

46
00:01:30,992 --> 00:01:32,012
and its source.

47
00:01:36,976 --> 00:01:39,146
Leads get a Decision Radar for every

48
00:01:39,186 --> 00:01:40,816
project: the open conflicts,

49
00:01:40,856 --> 00:01:42,776
the evidence, and who is affected.

50
00:01:42,816 --> 00:01:44,656
And every result is indexed,

51
00:01:44,696 --> 00:01:47,476
so precedentConflicts > 0 works in JQL,

52
00:01:47,516 --> 00:01:49,566
filters and dashboards.

53
00:01:51,916 --> 00:01:53,476
Precedent also exposes

54
00:01:53,516 --> 00:01:56,166
the same actions as MCP tools.

55
00:01:56,206 --> 00:01:57,856
Any team can add them to its own

56
00:01:57,896 --> 00:01:59,586
agents in Rovo Studio.

57
00:01:59,626 --> 00:02:01,576
Here, a custom Architecture Guard

58
00:02:01,616 --> 00:02:03,126
agent checks a planned change,

59
00:02:03,166 --> 00:02:04,646
finds the decision it would break,

60
00:02:04,686 --> 00:02:07,366
and proposes a compliant design instead.

61
00:02:07,406 --> 00:02:08,926
An open-source skill file brings

62
00:02:08,966 --> 00:02:11,076
the same check to coding agents.

63
00:02:17,411 --> 00:02:19,631
Everything lives in one decision log,

64
00:02:19,671 --> 00:02:21,161
in Confluence and Jira,

65
00:02:21,201 --> 00:02:22,931
with editable guardrails, history,

66
00:02:22,971 --> 00:02:24,851
exceptions and supersession,

67
00:02:24,891 --> 00:02:26,771
plus one-click sample content,

68
00:02:26,811 --> 00:02:29,641
so a new team sees value in a minute.

69
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:33,234
Precedent. One Forge app across Jira,

70
00:02:33,274 --> 00:02:35,534
Confluence, Rovo and MCP,

71
00:02:35,574 --> 00:02:37,644
so your team, and your agents,

72
00:02:37,684 --> 00:02:39,684
know what has already been decided.

